;; THE AUTHORED PACK CATALOGUE (K1, D900; pkg1 section 3, D885, D896). The one source of every model pack emon knows: id, revision, engine, kind, languages and
;; scripts, files with SHA-256 and byte count, licence and upstream. `bb packs --emit` generates kin/packdata.kin (what kin resolves and every host verifies
;; against) and release/packs/packs.json (for hooks and tools); `bb packs --emit --check` is the drift gate, run by `bb ci core`.
;;
;;   :id        <engine>-<variant>-<lang|role>; unique; a pack is immutable and superseded, never mutated (a changed byte is a new :rev, and its hash a new identity)
;;   :engine    a name of kin's engine table (`en` in kin/engines.kin), or :any for a pack every engine may read (a lexicon)
;;   :kind      :recognizer (per language), :osd, :detector, :classifier, :lexicon (`pkind` in kin/engines.kin)
;;   :langs     the language codes emon packs into one cell: the REQUEST's three letters (ISO 639-3, and emon.ocrtess's `chs`/`cht` for Chinese), recognizers only
;;   :scripts   ISO 15924, as emon.ocrport names them
;;   :files     the bytes a pack is: file name, SHA-256 of the file, its size
;;
;; ABSORBED: tools/tessdata/models.edn (tessdata_fast) and tools/ppocr/assets.edn (PP-OCRv5 mobile). Those two files STAY, byte for byte, as the pinned INPUTS of the
;; Tesseract and PP requested identities (tools/tessdata/identity.clj and tools/ppocr/identity.clj hash them into the policy cells every transcript is keyed by);
;; `bb packs --check` holds them to this catalogue, entry by entry, so there is one set of numbers and a disagreement fails. Retiring them is an identity
;; re-key (every transcript), which K1 does not do.
